{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_bdrk_zdlhrskbqr6tu7tcpnohtxm6lkftarlhugdvumptjmhu4mwucq5q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 7 tests pass with `--test-threads=1`. The issue was test parallelism: even though my mutex serialized the captures within our own tests, when multiple tests run in parallel, they all fight for fd 1 (which has been redirected). \n\nLet me improve the test setup so it doesn't depend on calling `cargo test` with a special flag. I'll force serial execution with a simpler approach - keep the mutex but also flush the test harness's internal stdout. Actually the real problem is: the test harness's reporting thread also writes to stdout. Let me think...\n\nActually, a simpler & more robust approach is to set the test harness to single-threaded by default. The standard way is to set `harness = false` and write our own runner, but easier: just use serial_test crate or accept that --test-threads=1 is needed.\n\nBest approach: since we already serialize via mutex, the test harness should still work. The remaining race is: thread A captures, thread B writes to stdout (test reporting), the writes go to the redirected fd. To prevent test-harness reporting from racing, the simplest is to require `--test-threads=1`.\n\nLet me document this and also try a different approach - make our capture use a child process. Actually that's overkill. Let me just configure the test harness to serial. We can use `#[serial]` from `serial_test` crate or just stick with --test-threads=1 and document.\n\nBetter yet: I can move the testing logic into a single test function and call it for all cases, so there's only one test:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":608,"cache_read_input_tokens":30127,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":608,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"43f08b2d-27b9-48a4-ad31-7c51bc8adb67","uuid":"01075615-d49b-4795-9f5f-704a9b2bc096"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_bdrk_zdlhrskbqr6tu7tcpnohtxm6lkftarlhugdvumptjmhu4mwucq5q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_0165Ghbkt5fJmUVfait6DZQi","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/tmp/harvest-work-Ky57Vr/translated_rust/tests/ffi_compare.rs","old_string":"#[test]\nfn driver_zero() {\n    compare_for(0);\n}\n\n#[test]\nfn driver_one() {\n    compare_for(1);\n}\n\n#[test]\nfn driver_small() {\n    for x in 0..16 {\n        compare_for(x);\n    }\n}\n\n#[test]\nfn driver_negative() {\n    // C: for-loop with i=0, condition i<x where x<=0 means no iterations;\n    // both should print nothing.\n    for x in [-1, -10, i32::MIN].iter() {\n        compare_for(*x);\n    }\n}\n\n#[test]\nfn driver_medium() {\n    compare_for(100);\n    compare_for(1000);\n}\n\n#[test]\nfn driver_large() {\n    // Larger value to exercise more iterations.\n    compare_for(10_000);\n}","new_string":"// Run all driver comparisons in a single #[test] to avoid concurrent\n// stdout-capture races with the test harness. Capturing stdout requires\n// dup2'ing fd 1, which is process-wide; running in parallel would corrupt\n// captured output. The mutex inside `capture_stdout` only protects against\n// our own functions racing — it cannot stop the test harness's own writes.\n#[test]\nfn driver_matches_c_for_all_inputs() {\n    // Edge case: x == 0 (no iterations).\n    compare_for(0);\n    // Edge case: x == 1 (one iteration).\n    compare_for(1);\n    // Small values 0..16.\n    for x in 0..16 {\n        compare_for(x);\n    }\n    // Negative values and INT_MIN — all yield zero iterations.\n    for x in [-1, -10, i32::MIN].iter() {\n        compare_for(*x);\n    }\n    // Medium values.\n    compare_for(100);\n    compare_for(1000);\n    // Larger value to exercise more iterations.\n    compare_for(10_000);\n}"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_